$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of N-(Quinolin-8-yl)thiophene-3-carboxamide. To a solution of
3-thiophenecarboxylic acid (1.92 g, 15 mmol) and DMF (5 drops) in DCM (30
mL) under N2 atmosphere, oxalyl chloride (1.4 mL, 16.5 mmol, 1.1 equiv)
was added dropwise at 0 °C. The mixture was stirred for 1.5 h at room
temperature, and then the solvent was evapotated in vacuum. Resulting
acid chloride was used immediately without further purification. A
solution of acid chloride in CH2Cl2 (10 mL) at 0 °C temperature was added
dropwise to the solution of 8-aminoquinoline (2.16 g, 19.5 mmol, 1.3
equiv) and Et3N (2.8 mL, 19.5 mmol, 1.3 equiv) in CH2Cl2 (30 mL), then
the solution was warmed to room temperature. After stirring overnight,
the reaction mixture was quenched with H2O (30 mL) and the organic layer
was separated. The aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 x 30 mL).
The combined organic phase was dried over MgSO4, filtered and evaporated.
Recrystallization from hexanes/EtOAc 4:1. 3.26 g (85%) of
N-(quinolin-8-yl)thiophene-3-carboxamide as a white solid. 1H-NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3, ppm) δ 10.50 (s, 1H), 8.84 (dd, J = 7.5, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 8.79
(dd, J = 4.2, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 8.15-8.11 (m, 2H), 7.65 (dd, J = 5.0, 1.3 Hz,
1H), 7.56-7.52 (m, 1H), 7.49 (dd, J = 8.3, 1.4 Hz, 1H), 7.43 (dd, J =
8.2, 4.2 Hz, 1H), 7.39 (dd, J = 5.1, 3.0 Hz, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Cobalt-Promoted Dimerization of Aminoquinoline Benzamides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Grigorjeva, Liene; Daugulis, Olafs
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2015), 17(5), 1204-1207

