$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure H for the Preparation of
Benzanilide Inhibitor Intermediates: To a scintillation vial equipped
with a stir bar was combined the amine (0.15 mmol, 1.0 equiv) and the Boc
protected acid coupling partner (59 mg, 0.29 mmol, 2.0 equiv) in THF
(0.50 mL, 0.30 M). EDCI hydrochloride (29 mg, 0.15 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was
subsequently added. The reaction progress was monitored by LC-MS.
Complete conversion of the amine starting material to product was
observed after approximately 1 h. The solvent was removed under reduced
pressure, and the crude residue was then dissolved in a 1:1 mixture of
TFA:CH2Cl2 (4.0 mL total). After 1 h, the solvent was removed and the
crude residue was lyophilized for one hour to remove trace TFA. The crude
amines were used without further purification. General Warhead Addition
Procedure I for the Preparation of Inhibitors The crude amines were
dissolved in MeOH at a concentration of 0.10 M in a round bottom flask
equipped with a stir bar. Triethylamine (4.0 equiv) was added to the
reaction mixture. Ethyl 2-chloroacetimidate hydrochloride (4.0 equiv) was
subsequently added, and the mixture was stirred at rt until completion as
determined by LC-MS (20 min to 1 h). The solvent was removed, and
purification by reverse-phase column chromatography (gradient: 10% MeCN
to 100% MeCN in H2O + 0.1% TFA) followed by subsequent lyophilization.
The products as TFA salts. Inhibitor 5b: Coupling of commercially
available benzylamine by procedure H, followed by warhead addition by
procedure I. Inhibitor 18b: Coupling of commercially available
3-phenylbenzylamine by procedure H, followed by warhead addition by
procedure I. 18b in 79% overall yield. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CD3OD d-4): δ
7.60-7.26 (m, 9H), 4.44 (s, 2H), 4.36 (s, 2H), 3.35 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H),
2.39 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 1.96 (quin, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H). 13C-NMR (100 MHz,
CD3OD): δ 174.64, 164.71, 142.78, 142.19, 140.51, 130.08, 129.85, 128.43,
127.96, 127.55, 127.29, 126.92, 44.23, 43.36, 40.06, 33.14, 24.30. HRMS
(For C19H23ClN3O, MH+): Calc’d 344.1530, found 344.1529.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM HPLC purification (final stage)
